         "Doctor, Medicare doesn't let us bill chondroplasty and meniscectomy together in the same knee. We had to remove the chondroplasty code.",
         "Blunt and lacks clinical detail regarding anatomical compartments, making the surgeon feel their work is being arbitrarily dismissed.",
         "Dear Dr. Harrison,\n\nThank you for reaching out regarding the billing for encounter #93821 (Left knee arthroscopy). Under CMS National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) policy and AAOS guidelines, chondroplasty (CPT 29877) is bundled into a meniscectomy (CPT 29881) when performed in the same anatomical compartment (the medial compartment). Payers consider debridement in the operative field as inherent to the primary procedure.\n\nHowever, if significant chondroplasty was performed in a *separate, distinct* compartment of the knee (such as the patellofemoral or lateral compartment), CPT guidelines permit reporting HCPCS code G0289 for the separate compartment service. If your operative findings substantiate work in a separate compartment, please update the operative report to specify the distinct anatomical location, and we will gladly resubmit the claim with appropriate documentation.\n\nSincerely,\nHospital Surgical Coding Team",
